      "text": "If the printer prints 17 pages per minute, we can first determine how many pages will be printed in 1 minute by multiplying 17 pages per minute by the number of minutes it takes to print those pages. Since we want to find how many minutes it will take to print 200 pages, we can then divide the total number of pages by the number of pages that can be printed per minute. It may be difficult to use long division to divide 200 by 17 exactly, so we can first find the nearest multiple of 17 that is less or equal to 200.\n\n          12 --- 17 goes 5 times into 17 times 12, yielding 17, and leaving a remainder of 11\n\n12 * 17 = 204 (17 + 1) * 12\n\nSo 12 + 17 = 29 gives us 29 * 17 approaches 205 but is greater than 200... thus 28 * 17 will give us 28 * 17 = 476 = 200 + 224\n\n28 * 17 goes 14 times into 102 times 28, yielding 102, and leaving a remainder of 4\n\nSo we have 476 - 476 = 0 pages remaining left to print!\n\nTherefore, it will take 28 minutes to print exactly 200 pages. The answer is 28.",
