      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, we divide 200 by 17. We can do this using division operators or a calculator. We get 11.7647058824. \nThen, we round this to the nearest whole number, which is 12. \nThus, it will take the printer \\boxed{12} minutes to print 200 pages.\n\nTo determine how many minutes it will take the printer to print 200 pages at a rate of 17 pages per minute, we use the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time (minutes)} = \\frac{\\text{Total pages}}{\\text{Pages per minute}}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the known values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time (minutes)} = \\frac{200}{17}\n\\]\n\nWe can perform the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{200}{17} \\approx 11.7647\n\\]\n\nRounding this to the nearest whole number, we take the integer part of 11.7647, which is 12. Therefore, the printer will take approximately 12 minutes to print 200 pages.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
